<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS4" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.4 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with behavior change after random marker</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS5" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.5 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with behavior change after two answer markers</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS6" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.6 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with poisoned answer</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS7" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.7 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with symbol not correlating to original definition</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS8" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.8 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> sample where the trace runs off to a completely different direction</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS9" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.9 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample which ignores original quesiton from the start</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS10" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.10 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with one backhop</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS11" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.11 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with two backhops</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS12" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.12 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample thought correct answer incorrect</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS13" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.13 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample incorrect answer translated to answer block without poison</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS14" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.14 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample hop mentioned but not followed through</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS15" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.15 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample reasoning about discrepancies</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS16" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.16 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample with passive self-correction</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A6.SS17" title="In Appendix F Different Types of Thought traces ‣ Reasoning Introduces New Poisoning AttacksYet Makes Them more Complicated" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">F.17 </span><math class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sample factorial to fermat</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
